  "findings": [
    {
      "evidence": "design.md says \"`EnvironmentFailure(WorkerError)` carries a condition id from the registry, and only a registered condition raises it\". In template/scripts/lifecycle_workers.py, `EnvironmentFailure.__init__(self, condition, message)` stores any string. worker_preflight.CONDITION_IDS is not consulted. Call sites such as `PostMergeEnvironmentError(\"process-tool\", ...)` and `@environment_condition(\"github-credential\")` use correct ids only by convention. A typo, or a future caller passing an unregistered id, would silently get free-of-charge release treatment.",
      "id": "environment-failure-unregistered-condition",
      "severity": "advisory",
      "summary": "The design says only a registered condition raises EnvironmentFailure, but the constructor does not check that rule. This weakens the guarantee that any other failure stays an ordinary failed run."
    }
  ],
